WEBVTT

00:00:09.331 --> 00:00:20.646
The Well by Claire Harris.

00:00:20.706 --> 00:00:22.847
It is summer.

00:00:22.907 --> 00:00:25.238
The air is hot.

00:00:25.298 --> 00:00:28.900
It is hot inside Leah's house.

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:35.913
Leah lives with her mother, her father, and her brother, Jay.

00:00:35.973 --> 00:00:39.275
Her grandmother lives with them too.

00:00:39.335 --> 00:00:43.610
Leah's grandmother is old and sick.

00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:46.892
She lies in her bed all day.

00:00:46.952 --> 00:00:49.714
The old woman is sad.

00:00:49.774 --> 00:00:52.468
Her husband is dead.

00:00:52.528 --> 00:00:56.010
She often talks to his photograph.

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:58.712
Yes, husband.

00:00:58.772 --> 00:01:02.366
Oh, it's in the well.

00:01:02.426 --> 00:01:05.508
It's in a bucket of water.

00:01:05.568 --> 00:01:07.748
Thank you.

00:01:07.808 --> 00:01:12.408
Leah and her mother are in grandmother's room.

00:01:12.468 --> 00:01:16.280
Leah's mother brings some food and water.

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:20.212
Please, go to the well.

00:01:20.272 --> 00:01:22.054
Says grandmother.

00:01:22.114 --> 00:01:26.687
Bring me some water in the bucket.

00:01:26.746 --> 00:01:30.748
There is no well here, Ma.

00:01:30.808 --> 00:01:32.860
Says Leah's mother.

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:35.912
You live in the town now.

00:01:35.971 --> 00:01:38.486
We have good water.

00:01:38.546 --> 00:01:41.612
It comes from the tap.

00:01:41.672 --> 00:01:46.374
Leah's mother speaks quietly to her daughter.

00:01:46.434 --> 00:01:50.416
Grandmother is sick, she says.

00:01:50.476 --> 00:01:54.318
She is not thinking clearly.

00:01:54.378 --> 00:01:59.190
Leah's mother gives the old woman some water.

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:02.492
No, no.

00:02:02.551 --> 00:02:04.402
Says grandmother.

00:02:04.462 --> 00:02:08.558
Go to the farms well.

00:02:08.618 --> 00:02:14.164
We must not visit the old farm now, Ma.

00:02:14.224 --> 00:02:16.214
Lea's mother says.

00:02:16.274 --> 00:02:19.576
The farm is near the volcano.

00:02:19.636 --> 00:02:22.698
The volcano is dangerous.

00:02:22.758 --> 00:02:25.599
There is fire and smoke.

00:02:25.659 --> 00:02:29.471
Soldiers are guarding the roads.

00:02:29.530 --> 00:02:32.552
Grandmother doesn't hear her.

00:02:32.612 --> 00:02:35.474
Go to the well.

00:02:35.534 --> 00:02:37.988
Grandmother says again.

00:02:38.047 --> 00:02:41.461
Bring me the bucket of water.

00:02:41.521 --> 00:02:43.953
Please hurry.

00:02:44.012 --> 00:02:45.683
I'll go.

00:02:45.743 --> 00:02:47.164
says Leah.

00:02:47.224 --> 00:02:49.474
I'll walk to the farm.

00:02:49.534 --> 00:02:51.886
I know the way.

00:02:51.945 --> 00:02:56.868
Leah tells her father and brother about the well.

00:02:56.927 --> 00:03:00.219
Leah, you mustn't visit the farm.

00:03:00.279 --> 00:03:03.180
The volcano is near the farm.

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:06.856
The volcano is dangerous.

00:03:06.915 --> 00:03:09.560
I'll go with Leah.

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:13.662
We'll get the water for grandmother.

00:03:13.722 --> 00:03:19.153
The next morning, Leah and Jay get up early.

00:03:19.213 --> 00:03:23.514
Leah puts some bread and a sausage in her bag.

00:03:23.574 --> 00:03:28.435
She puts a bottle of water in the bag too.

00:03:28.495 --> 00:03:32.776
Jay and Leah are on the highway.

00:03:32.836 --> 00:03:34.706
The air is hot.

00:03:34.766 --> 00:03:38.019
The air is full of dust.

00:03:38.079 --> 00:03:43.174
At the checkpoint, Leah and Jay meet a soldier.

00:03:43.234 --> 00:03:45.136
He talks to them.

00:03:45.195 --> 00:03:48.878
The volcano isn't dangerous today.

00:03:48.938 --> 00:03:53.001
We're going to our grandmother's farm.

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:55.002
She's sick.

00:03:55.062 --> 00:03:57.995
She wants water from the well.

00:03:58.054 --> 00:04:00.746
It will cure her sickness.

00:04:00.806 --> 00:04:03.968
You're going to get some magic water.

00:04:04.028 --> 00:04:06.638
Bring me some, too.

00:04:06.698 --> 00:04:10.748
Leah and Jay stop next to a bridge.

00:04:10.808 --> 00:04:13.189
They eat their lunch.

00:04:13.249 --> 00:04:17.240
There is a small house next to the bridge.

00:04:17.300 --> 00:04:20.041
A friendly woman lives there.

00:04:20.102 --> 00:04:23.192
She talks to Jay and Leah.

00:04:23.252 --> 00:04:25.703
She has a small dog.

00:04:25.763 --> 00:04:28.874
It is a small red dog.

00:04:28.934 --> 00:04:32.466
Jay gives the dog some sausage.

00:04:32.525 --> 00:04:35.117
Where are you going?

00:04:35.176 --> 00:04:36.845
The woman asks.

00:04:36.904 --> 00:04:39.732
It is a hot day.

00:04:39.792 --> 00:04:43.503
We're going to our grandmother's farm.

00:04:43.563 --> 00:04:45.194
Jay replies.

00:04:45.254 --> 00:04:46.984
She is sick.

00:04:47.044 --> 00:04:50.095
She wants water from the well.

00:04:50.155 --> 00:04:53.205
Take some water from my well.

00:04:53.265 --> 00:04:54.586
It's good.

00:04:54.646 --> 00:04:57.766
It's good fresh water.

00:04:57.826 --> 00:05:01.027
That's a good idea, Leah.

00:05:01.087 --> 00:05:03.698
It's a very hot day.

00:05:03.758 --> 00:05:06.726
I don't want to walk anymore.

00:05:06.786 --> 00:05:10.807
Okay Jay, stay here.

00:05:10.867 --> 00:05:14.979
I will go to the farm alone.

00:05:15.039 --> 00:05:18.321
Leah walks on.

00:05:18.381 --> 00:05:21.853
After a minute, Jay follows her.

00:05:21.913 --> 00:05:24.734
They walk and they walk.

00:05:24.794 --> 00:05:27.346
There are no houses here.

00:05:27.406 --> 00:05:29.648
There are no animals.

00:05:29.708 --> 00:05:34.120
There is dry grass and there is dust.

00:05:34.180 --> 00:05:36.854
They hear a sound.

00:05:36.914 --> 00:05:39.428
What is that sound?

00:05:39.488 --> 00:05:41.278
Jay asks.

00:05:41.338 --> 00:05:44.160
Is someone calling us?

00:05:44.220 --> 00:05:46.052
No.

00:05:46.112 --> 00:05:49.044
It's the sound of the wind.

00:05:49.104 --> 00:05:50.896
Leah replies.

00:05:50.956 --> 00:05:52.196
No.

00:05:52.256 --> 00:05:54.478
It isn't the wind.

00:05:54.537 --> 00:05:56.590
It's a ghost.

00:05:56.650 --> 00:05:59.482
I'm afraid of ghosts.

00:05:59.542 --> 00:06:03.124
There are no ghosts here.

00:06:03.184 --> 00:06:06.680
Leah and Jay are at the farm.

00:06:06.740 --> 00:06:09.916
Jay sees oranges on a tree.

00:06:09.976 --> 00:06:13.028
He doesn't see any ghosts.

00:06:13.088 --> 00:06:17.380
He pulls some oranges from the tree.

00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:21.402
Leah and Jay find the well.

00:06:21.462 --> 00:06:24.004
Its cover is broken.

00:06:24.064 --> 00:06:26.876
Jay lifts the cover.

00:06:26.936 --> 00:06:31.158
The water doesn't smell good.

00:06:31.218 --> 00:06:35.660
This water is bad, Leah.

00:06:35.720 --> 00:06:37.368
Jay says.

00:06:37.428 --> 00:06:41.586
We must take some water for grandmother.

00:06:41.646 --> 00:06:43.476
Leah replies.

00:06:43.536 --> 00:06:46.746
We must get the bucket.

00:06:46.806 --> 00:06:50.587
We must pull this rope.

00:06:50.647 --> 00:06:53.168
They hold the rope.

00:06:53.228 --> 00:06:56.198
They pull and they pull.

00:06:56.258 --> 00:06:59.599
The bucket is very heavy.

00:06:59.659 --> 00:07:04.080
At last, the bucket is out of the well.

00:07:04.140 --> 00:07:07.570
It is full of dirty water.

00:07:07.630 --> 00:07:10.742
Leah empties the bucket.

00:07:10.802 --> 00:07:18.214
Jay and Leah have a surprise.

00:07:18.274 --> 00:07:24.057
Gold!

00:07:24.117 --> 00:07:28.129
These are gold coins!

00:07:28.188 --> 00:07:30.119
Yes!

00:07:30.179 --> 00:07:32.620
I remember these.

00:07:32.680 --> 00:07:36.622
They are Grandfather's coins.

00:07:36.682 --> 00:07:41.142
Leah and Jay are carrying the bucket.

00:07:41.202 --> 00:07:42.893
It is heavy.

00:07:42.953 --> 00:07:46.184
There are lots of oranges in the bucket.

00:07:46.244 --> 00:07:50.794
The gold coins are under the oranges.

00:07:50.854 --> 00:07:55.905
Jay and Leah meet a gang of boys near the bridge.

00:07:55.965 --> 00:07:58.876
What's in your bucket?

00:07:58.936 --> 00:08:01.106
The boys shout.

00:08:01.166 --> 00:08:03.477
Ah, oranges!

00:08:03.537 --> 00:08:05.648
Give them to us!

00:08:05.708 --> 00:08:09.871
The small red dog runs out of the house.

00:08:09.931 --> 00:08:12.751
He barks at the gang of boys.

00:08:12.811 --> 00:08:15.872
He barks and he barks.

00:08:15.932 --> 00:08:19.463
The friendly woman comes out of the house.

00:08:19.523 --> 00:08:21.413
The boys run away.

00:08:21.433 --> 00:08:26.354
Jay and Leah are at the checkpoint.

00:08:26.414 --> 00:08:29.435
The soldier looks in the bucket.

00:08:29.495 --> 00:08:33.066
You don't have any magic water?

00:08:33.126 --> 00:08:34.794
No!

00:08:34.854 --> 00:08:40.004
We have some magic oranges.

00:08:40.064 --> 00:08:45.848
Leah and Jay give the soldier some oranges.

00:08:45.908 --> 00:08:50.020
The soldier smiles at them.

00:08:50.080 --> 00:08:54.282
Leah and Jay are at home now.

00:08:54.342 --> 00:08:57.744
Their grandmother is lying in her bed.

00:08:57.804 --> 00:09:01.607
Is that my bucket of water?

00:09:01.627 --> 00:09:02.944
No.

00:09:03.004 --> 00:09:09.184
It's grandfather's gold.

00:09:09.244 --> 00:09:13.848
Everybody laughs.

00:09:13.908 --> 00:09:16.299
They are very happy.

00:09:16.359 --> 00:09:19.742
Grandmother looks at her husband's photo.

00:09:19.802 --> 00:09:21.842
She smiles.

00:09:21.902 --> 00:09:25.756
Suddenly, they hear a sound.

00:09:25.816 --> 00:09:28.077
Is it the sound of the wind?
